<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Saxe-Gotha</h1><p class="st-meta">1640 CE – 1825 CE · capital Gotha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ernestine Saxon duchy in Thuringia whose founder, Ernest the Pious, made it a model of Lutheran school reform and orderly government.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> was created in 1640 when the Ernestine lands of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> were divided among the brothers of the ducal house, and Ernest I received Gotha. He built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedenstein-palace">Friedenstein Palace</a> as his residence. In 1672 he inherited Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a>, and the state became known as Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha">Ernest the Pious</a> introduced compulsory schooling, a famous school method and detailed church and state ordinances, rebuilding a land ruined by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. On his death in 1675 his lands were divided among seven sons, creating the duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiningen">Meiningen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romhild">Römhild</a>, Eisenberg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildburghausen">Hildburghausen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-ii-duke-of-saxe-gotha-altenburg">Ernest II</a>, in the 18th century, was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a> who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seeberg-observatory">Seeberg</a> observatory.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The line died out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iv-duke-of-saxe-gotha-altenburg">Duke Frederick IV</a> in 1825. In the redistribution of 1826 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> went to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-coburg-and-gotha">Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld</a>, forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-saxe-coburg-and-gotha">Duchy of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a> became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-saxe-altenburg">Duchy of Saxe-Altenburg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-saxe-gotha.jpg" alt="Duchy of Saxe-Gotha" width="320" height="262"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SajoniaGotha1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1640 CE – 1825 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gotha</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ernest I the Pious, Frederick II, Ernest II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg, Sachsen-Gotha-Altenburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1732&amp;focus=duchy-of-saxe-gotha" aria-label="Duchy of Saxe-Gotha on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4924 411 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Saxe-Gotha lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5244 667L5257 666M5244 667L5229 694M5244 667L5199 691M5244 667L5251 687M5244 667L5251 687M5244 667L5238 678M5244 667L5245 682M5244 667L5241 683M5244 667L5271 666"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5257 666h0M5229 694h0M5199 691h0M5251 687h0M5251 687h0M5238 678h0M5245 682h0M5241 683h0M5271 666h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5244 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d=